% The home's world readings: the declarations every package that reads them includes (the
% pattern 'Interface package': one owner for a pred that crosses packages). Declarations only.
% The host publishes each family below with exactly one member true per role, every beat
% ('Complementary readings', 'Exclusive family, single reason'); a sensor not yet wired is a
% member of its own (unsensed), so a rule that needs the reading does not fire (the safe failure).
catalog home_world 1.
include "home_map.llp".

namespace home produce (dyn).

type scene {home night away}.
bwd other(scene, scene).
other(home, night).
other(home, away).
other(night, home).
other(night, away).
other(away, home).
other(away, night).
% the home's mode and mood as the world holds them (a Metis conclusion of the scenes package: the mode and mood
% ports, nina-live's redesign step 3): levels every package reads, each keeping its own latch of the last swept
type sure {no yes}.
type mood {calm cozy focus lively sleep wake none}.
pred home_mode(sure, scene) : home.
pred home_mood(sure, mood) : home.
pred mode_b(scene) : home.        % the beliefs on the world's ports mode and mood (one key per value), quantised by the levels
pred mood_b(mood) : home.
bwd othermood(mood, mood).
pred swept(scene) : home.          % a package's latch: the mode it last swept for
pred moodseen(mood) : home.        % … the mood it last expressed
othermood(calm, cozy).
othermood(calm, focus).
othermood(calm, lively).
othermood(calm, sleep).
othermood(calm, wake).
othermood(cozy, calm).
othermood(cozy, focus).
othermood(cozy, lively).
othermood(cozy, sleep).
othermood(cozy, wake).
othermood(focus, calm).
othermood(focus, cozy).
othermood(focus, lively).
othermood(focus, sleep).
othermood(focus, wake).
othermood(lively, calm).
othermood(lively, cozy).
othermood(lively, focus).
othermood(lively, sleep).
othermood(lively, wake).
othermood(sleep, calm).
othermood(sleep, cozy).
othermood(sleep, focus).
othermood(sleep, lively).
othermood(sleep, wake).
othermood(wake, calm).
othermood(wake, cozy).
othermood(wake, focus).
othermood(wake, lively).
othermood(wake, sleep).
othermood(none, calm).
othermood(none, cozy).
othermood(none, focus).
othermood(none, lively).
othermood(none, sleep).
othermood(none, wake).

% presence per room (the mmWave radar; not yet wired: unsensed)
pred occupied(room) : home.
pred empty(room) : home.          % nobody now, not long enough to be vacant
pred vacant(room) : home.         % nobody for vacant_after_s (the host's timer, never a counter in the rules)
pred unsensed(room) : home.       % no presence sensor in the room
% the whole home
pred someone_home : home.
pred nobody_home : home.
pred home_unsensed : home.
% time of day (sun.sun)
pred day : home.
pred night : home.
% the ventilation units' state, read by the packages that advise about air
pred running(unit) : home.
pred stopped(unit) : home.
pred heater_on(unit) : home.
pred heater_off(unit) : home.
pred unit_ok(unit) : home.
pred unit_missing(unit) : home.   % the unit does not answer in Home Assistant
% a unit's power as the semantic world believes it (metis-lang spec/16 §3-4: the belief on_b on the
% world's port `unit_on` (the units' power; light_on and tv_on are the other kinds'), quantised by the level `power` a package declares in its domain.yaml's beliefs: and
% levels:). The host asserts exactly one level atom per unit the world knows: on / off when a reading
% confirms it (p >= 0.95 / p < 0.05); unconfirmed in between, i.e. the host commanded it and no reading
% has confirmed it yet, or the unit stopped answering and the belief is forgetting. A unit the world does
% not know holds no atom. running | stopped stay the likeliest reading: a refusal names stopped(U) as
% its blocker (the replier matches a blocker by its pred), the level says how sure the home is.
pred on_b(unit) : home.
type power_level {off unconfirmed on}.
pred power(power_level, unit) : home.

% events: the host asserts each for one beat, on the edge it names
pred entered(room) : home.        % the room became occupied
pred left_home : home.            % someone_home -> nobody_home
pred came_home : home.            % nobody_home -> someone_home
pred dawn : home.                 % the sun rose
